Iceberg by Otavio Good
https://github.com/libretro/glsl-shaders/blob/master/procedural/otaviogood-iceberg.glsl
(the original shader in its libretro / RetroArch form, commit 7e77d928 of
libretro/glsl-shaders; the raw file is
https://raw.githubusercontent.com/libretro/glsl-shaders/master/procedural/otaviogood-iceberg.glsl)

The licence statement that covers this shader is in the shader file's own
header comment (lines 105 to 111 of that file), signed by the author. It reads:

    License CC0 - http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/
    To the extent possible under law, the author(s) have dedicated all
    copyright and related and neighboring rights to this software to the public
    domain worldwide. This software is distributed without any warranty.
    ^ This means do ANYTHING YOU WANT with this code. Because we are
    programmers, not lawyers.
    -Otavio Good

(The line breaks above are only wrapped for this page; the quoted text is
unchanged. The same header is kept at the top of main.metal.) The libretro
glsl-shaders repository has no repository-wide LICENSE file, so this per-file
statement is the one that applies.

Ported to Metal Shading Language for MacOS Live Wallpaper; see the note at the
top of main.metal for what was changed. In short:

  - The libretro wrapper (vertex shader, uniforms, parameter pragma, main()) is
    removed; time comes from iTime and the size from iResolution.
  - Animation runs at half the libretro speed (the libretro wrapper ran it at
    1.5 times Shadertoy speed; here it is 0.5 times), so the camera drifts
    calmly on a desktop.
  - The "fade" value the author computes for each of the three camera shots,
    whose use was commented out at the end of RayTrace, is switched on, so the
    shots dissolve through black instead of cutting.
  - Out parameters are written thread T&; the locals named cos and sin in
    RotateX/Y/Z are renamed; variables are initialised.
  - The author's disabled options (non-realtime HQ renderer, manual camera,
    HQ noise) are removed.
  - Speed-ups that leave the picture unchanged, added to fit the wallpaper's
    GPU budget: a cheap bound that skips the iceberg's distance where it
    cannot matter, larger march steps for rays that cannot hit the water,
    ambient-occlusion and scattering work done only for the material that uses
    it, and one shared call for the camera ray and the reflection ray. Against
    the plain port, fewer than 0.02% of pixels differ by more than 2/255.
  - No images or other assets are used or shipped.

Apart from the items listed above (slower time, the fade between shots, the
removed options), the shader's maths, constants, camera path and colours are
the author's.

To the extent possible under law, the author has waived all copyright and
related rights to this work.

    CC0 1.0 Universal (CC0 1.0) Public Domain Dedication
    https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/
